From c19237265b00b844906b4fad2c9e8e7754706397 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:24:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] No E411 when saving a kit row whose sound has no params

A kit row's ParamManager can be without its collections (seen after a clip type change and an undo;
#4938's hard fault comes from the same state). Saving that row as a preset (its audition pad held +
SAVE) wrote the params through Sound::writeToFile() and froze with E411. Leave them out when the
ParamManager has none, as NoteRow::writeToFile() already does: the preset loads with default params.

Test: the random-input run seed 1011 (--mode deep, froze at input 177) now passes it.
---
 src/deluge/processing/sound/sound.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/processing/sound/sound.cpp b/src/deluge/processing/sound/sound.cpp
index cd98c149..89e289d9 100644
--- a/src/deluge/processing/sound/sound.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/processing/sound/sound.cpp
@@ -4245,7 +4245,10 @@ void Sound::writeToFile(Serializer& writer, bool savingSong, ParamManager* param
 	writer.writeAttribute("spread", unisonStereoSpread, false);
 	writer.closeTag();
 
-	if (paramManager) {
+	// A kit row's ParamManager can be without its collections (seen after undoing a change of the clip's type);
+	// writing the params then froze with E411. Leave them out as NoteRow::writeToFile() does: the sound loads with
+	// its default params rather than the Deluge freezing
+	if (paramManager && paramManager->containsAnyMainParamCollections()) {
 		writer.writeOpeningTagBeginning("defaultParams", true);
 		Sound::writeParamsToFile(writer, paramManager, false);
 		writer.writeClosingTag("defaultParams", true, true);
-- 
